1dc3`.\n\n## The blocking finding is genuinely closed\n\nThe cycle-1 verdict said admitting schema 8 removed the accident that used to stop an enforced script command, so `valid-script-worker-enforced.json` installed a plain shim and ran package code with the caller's full ambient authority. The fix landed exactly where that verdict said it belonged:\n\n- `skillspec.Load` **still accepts** the manifest — all 66 `agent-skill-v8` cases resolve correctly.\n- Admission moved into a new `internal/scriptpolicy` owning `script_execution_policy_unsupported` with the profile's fixed `unsupported`/`error` pair (checked against `profiles/manager.md:901`, both values match).\n- Two consumers: `skillcheck` (project install, global install, `curator skill check` — `error` severity aborts before any staging) and `install.activeScriptCommands` (the shim writer itself).\n\nI re-ran the mutation matrix rather than trusting it:\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| both guards active | pass |\n| `skillcheck` disabled | pass — shim writer catches |\n| shim writer disabled | pass — `skillcheck` catches |\n| **both disabled** | **FAIL** — `Status:ok`, launcher published |\n\nBoth-disabled reproduces the original regression byte for byte, so neither layer is decoration.\n\nAlso verified there's no remaining path to an uncontained shim (`stageRuntimeAndShims` is the only producer, both callers behind `validateNodes`; `globalbins` only mirrors already-published canonical shims), that `Enforced()` can't catch a `go-v1` build command (compiled `manager-worker-v1` lives on a different type), and that curator emits `conformance_claim none`, so nothing claims what this refusal denies.\n\nThe non-blocking fixture finding is fixed too — I instrumented the family and printed the real rejection reason for all 66 cases; every invalid case now fails for its own rule.\n\n## Gates (mine, standalone, at `77aafa0`)\n\ngofmt clean · `go build` 0 · `go vet` 0 · golangci-lint 2.12.2 \"0 issues\" · gate-selftest 81/0 · candidate `test-gate.sh` with `CI_REQUIRE_FULL_ROOT=1` **exit 0**, `served=43 deferred=0 excluded=0` (43 not 42 — `internal/scriptpolicy` is served), 10 skips all pre-existing classes.\n\nRemote: PR #34 11/11 default lanes (Race is ubuntu+macos by design, so 11 is the complete set), plus dispatched run `32668086905` on `a74f1f5` — 14/14 including **Candidate suite on all three OSes**, with `CANDIDATE_REF=6001dc3…` read out of the job log.\n\n## Carried forward — nothing blocking, nothing owned\n\n1. `profiles/manager.md:1008` makes the audit warning classes `script-command-declared-only` / `script-command-unfiltered-declared-network` REQUIRED; neither string exists in the tree. **Not** a regression here (the first applies to schema ≤7 too, the second is unreachable while enforced commands are refused) — but no board item owns it.\n2. The marker v3/v4 cross-field gap still has no board item, as cycle 1 required.\n3. The two guards differ in scope on purpose: `skillcheck` refuses a *declared* enforced command, the shim writer only an *active* one. Fail-closed, can't regress anything since schema 8 is new.\n4. Pre-existing repo-wide doc staleness: `README.md:36` still says \"schemas 1 through 5\" while `SupportedSchemaVersions` spans 1–8; CHANGELOG `Unreleased` empty after 68 commits.\n\nVerdict artifact `TASK-260823-1vleh5_review-verdict-rework.md` attached, notes recorded, logbook entry 0132 added. No `commit_ack` supplied — reviewer archetype, and `a74f1f5` is already on main. The story rolled back to `backlog` since its two remaining tasks (`1wvgw8`, `2u5xov`) are still there — expected board behaviour, not a demotion of this work.","ttft_ms":4453,"ttft_stream_ms":3652,"time_to_request_ms":57,"type":"result","duration_ms":924609,"uuid":"30a50d53-cc67-48ea-9f78-a9cb3bbd7c1a"}
